soundfonts/
NEPTUNE.ISO
extracted/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/

# original bytes, written by the importer from your copy; see docs/port/FIDELITY.md
godot/tests/fixtures/original/

# files copied out of NEPTUNE.ISO on demand (tools/gamefiles.py materialize)
build/
iso/
iso.tmp/
prefix/
.claude/worktrees/

# --- THE LEGACY PACK: the original game, written by tools/import/import_all.py from YOUR copy of the game (docs/play/LEGACY.md) as loose
# files into the folder godot/packs/legacy (tools/import/common.py legacy_root), never committed. Everything in godot/packs/ is ignored except its README
# and the dev pack (godot/packs/dev/, ours: committed, ships with the game); any other pack folder you put there stays yours.
/godot/packs/*
!/godot/packs/README.md
!/godot/packs/dev/
# godot/data/ is the project's own data and is committed: the rule values and the durations, the creature scripts' annotations, the menu layout (the one file the importer
# writes there: it holds nothing of the game) and the sectors and campaigns of your own. The original's presentation (the cutscenes' choreography) is the legacy pack's.
# your own data about the legacy pack that holds the game's content (the hand corrections of the voice transcripts; tools/import/common.py LEGACY_AREA)
/godot/data/legacy/
# the references the snapshot test renders from its pictures
/godot/tests/snapshots/*.png
# A developer's own mise overrides (docs/SETUP.md)
mise.local.toml
# Pack files (`<id>.larissa`, pack_tool --export-pack --archive): a legacy one holds the original content
*.larissa

# The godot-sandbox extension that runs a mod pack (fetched, pinned: tools/fetch_sandbox.py, docs/SETUP.md)
/godot/addons/godot_sandbox/
